      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's getting closer to what I'm seeing. The idea of \"resilience\" being a codeword for an activated state is exactly the kind of thing I've been suspecting. \n\nBut \"a call to unity\" sounds too much like a public-facing explanation. If this is a real directive meant for an elite tier, it wouldn't be so obvious/platitudinous. It would be functional. \n\nLook at this other snippet from a different leader in the same week: \"The stability of our systems remains, as it were, the priority in these changing tides.\" \n\nIf \"as it were\" is the synchronization marker, and \"stability\" is the second anchor... compare the two. If \"resilience\" in the first one meant \"activate the asset,\" what is the specific operational directive being signaled here with \"stability\"? Try to find the specific, non-obvious command being passed between them.",
